  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.1.4 - Quiet ApiKey fallback\n- LogDBClient no longer warns when filling Log.ApiKey from options on the batch path.\n- Log.ApiKey is internal by design; the fallback is the intended code path, not a misuse.\n- Aligns LogDBClient with NativeProtocolClient, which already does this silently.\n- No behavior change; quieter logs.\n\nv5.1.1 - NuGet.org Release\n- Publishes the public package line to nuget.org for unauthenticated consumption\n- Keeps the AutoMapper-free client package as the active public release line\n- No breaking API changes\n\nv5.0.18 - Version Line Alignment\n- Aligns LogDB.Client version with current public 5.0.18 release train\n- Keeps metadata in sync with SDK integrations and docs\n- No breaking API changes\n\nv5.0.0 - Standalone Package\n- BREAKING: Package is now fully standalone with no external dependencies on LogDB.Shared\n- All models are now defined within the package\n- Clean public API surface - internal implementation details hidden\n- Ready for open source distribution\n- Maintains full backward compatibility for public APIs\n\nv4.0.10 - Previous Release\n- Bug fixes and stability improvements",
